WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.090
In Antigravity IDE

2
00:00:02.090 --> 00:00:05.320
we can install many MCP tools

3
00:00:05.320 --> 00:00:08.120
to help control different external software

4
00:00:08.420 --> 00:00:11.080
However after installing MCP tools

5
00:00:11.080 --> 00:00:14.080
they are usually enabled by default

6
00:00:14.420 --> 00:00:16.340
which leads to an issue

7
00:00:16.800 --> 00:00:19.290
every time we chat with AI

8
00:00:19.290 --> 00:00:24.520
the system automatically injects all MCP definitions into context

9
00:00:24.520 --> 00:00:26.820
consuming extra AI token quota

10
00:00:26.820 --> 00:00:28.350
In light of this problem

11
00:00:28.350 --> 00:00:31.610
when specific MCP tools are not needed

12
00:00:31.610 --> 00:00:33.320
we should turn them off

13
00:00:33.320 --> 00:00:35.100
to effectively reduce token usage

14
00:00:35.100 --> 00:00:40.390
While Antigravity IDE natively provides toggles for settings

15
00:00:40.390 --> 00:00:42.940
the built-in panel occasionally runs into bugs—

16
00:00:42.940 --> 00:00:47.100
such as failing to list all installed MCP tools

17
00:00:47.100 --> 00:00:50.520
or disappearing entirely when checking connection errors

18
00:00:50.520 --> 00:00:55.400
To solve this I developed a dedicated native MCP Manager extension

19
00:00:55.680 --> 00:00:59.380
Once installed it displays in the IDE left sidebar

20
00:00:59.380 --> 00:01:01.480
providing many practical workflow features

21
00:01:01.880 --> 00:01:04.160
You can test connection health with 1-click

22
00:01:04.160 --> 00:01:07.200
or toggle all servers ON or OFF instantly

23
00:01:07.560 --> 00:01:11.330
This way during different AI tasks and conversations

24
00:01:11.330 --> 00:01:14.920
we can quickly enable or disable the corresponding MCP tools
